WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.070
A factory says its bags hold
five hundred grams on average.

2
00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:05.840
No machine is perfect.

3
00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:10.630
Single bag masses vary, with a
standard deviation of eight grams.

4
00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:13.160
An inspector weighs thirty bags.

5
00:00:13.210 --> 00:00:16.260
Their mean is four hundred
and ninety-seven grams.

6
00:00:16.310 --> 00:00:18.290
Only three grams short.

7
00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:20.230
Is that just normal variation?

8
00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:22.900
Or should the inspector be suspicious?

9
00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:26.760
In this mission, you'll treat the
sample mean as a random variable,

10
00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:29.140
with a normal distribution of its own.

11
00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:33.250
You'll see why averages vary
much less than single values.

12
00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:37.030
And you'll test at a significance
level, such as five per cent,

13
00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:39.790
to decide what counts as suspicious.

14
00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:44.230
Your mission: decide whether that average
of four hundred and ninety-seven grams

15
00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:45.400
is suspicious.
